 "description": "Find out how many versions of each event type are actually in flight. Reports a type arriving at more than one version in a single batch, which means every consumer must handle all of them at once, versions outside the set you support, and supported versions nothing produces - handling carried for nothing is still a cost. Pay 120000 atomic USDC on Base via exact x402. MCP does not pay; it provides a challenge handoff.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "events": {
    "description": "A batch of records as JSON objects, at most 2000. Nothing is fetched, delivered or acknowledged, and no signature or secret is handled.",
    "example": [
     {
      "event_id": "evt-1",
      "offset": 101,
      "order_id": "o-1",
      "schema_version": "2",
      "stream": "orders-0",
      "total": 42.5,
      "type": "order.created"
